Z||000000||Raven01||11-23-2001||09:54 PM||||I have a couple of quick questions.  I just purchased a 86 Fiero 4cl with 24k original miles.  I am having a problem with the front brakes sticking and the headlights not going up.  I can hear the motor turning on the headlights, but they don't move.  Any suggestions on either of the problems would be greatly appreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gary W||11-23-2001||10:06 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  for headlight repair kits (broken gears). Your best bet for the brakes is to replace the front calipers with rebuilts. Try your local auto parts store or Autozone.com<P>Good luck, and welcome to the forum!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||11-24-2001||06:17 AM||||I just ordered a headlight motor gear from Rodney (about 10 minutes ago).  Great guy to work with.  (Headlight motor just went out as I turned off my lights after work this morning.  Original motor, too.  At least it's never been rebuilt--no idea how many miles are on it.)||||reg||1
